   "source": [
    "## The CIFAR10 dataset"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "54041fc6",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "The dataset consistes of 60000 32x32 color images in 10 classes: plane, car, bird, cat, deer, dog, frog, horse, ship, truck, with 6000 images per class. This dataset can be downloaded directly from `PyTorch` using the `torchvision` module.  \n",
    "So the original images are 32x32x3 arrays. The third dimension corresponds to color (red, green, blue). Ofcourse, it has to be turned into `PyTorch` tensors. Also, it is more convenient to scale them [-1, 1]. It can be achieved using a transformation\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
<<<<<<< HEAD
   "execution_count": 26,
=======
   "execution_count": 1,
>>>>>>> 1a27d747aca581f8916281d950ec89675de3a0c7
   "id": "a42f2f8d",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import torch\n",
    "import torchvision\n",
    "import torchvision.transforms as transforms\n",
    "\n",
    "# Transform to be applied to each imager\n",
    "transform = transforms.Compose([transforms.ToTensor(), # This turns the picture to a Tensor\n",
    " transforms.Normalize((0.5, 0.5, 0.5), (0.5, 0.5, 0.5))]) # This scales it to [-1, 1]\n",
    "\n",
    "# Here is how to load train dataset\n",
    "trainset = torchvision.datasets.CIFAR10(root = '../data', train=True,\n",
    "                                        download=False, transform=transform)\n",
    "# And for loading test dataset\n",
    "testset = torchvision.datasets.CIFAR10(root='../data', train=False,\n",
    "                                       download=False, transform=transform)\n",
    "\n",
    " # These are the class labels\n",
    "classes = ('plane', 'car', 'bird', 'cat',\n",
    " 'deer', 'dog', 'frog', 'horse', 'ship', 'truck')"
   ]
  },
